1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Эрик Акселевич Бергбом, Erik Bergbom (6.10.1884, Бернеборг, Вел. Кн. Финляндское - ?)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://russianestonia.eu/index.php?title=%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D0%AD%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BA_%D0%90%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT The son of Axel Gabriel Bergbom (24.10.1948, Helsingfors - 24.10.1900) and his wife Selma Ingeborg (18.11.1853, Kokkola, Finland - 7.02.1937), nee Oberg (Öberg). Lieutenant. In the Great War, he was sent to the Thessaloniki Front,
2 CONC  a pilot of the 521st and 525th squadrons of the Serbian army.
2 CONT He joined the North-Western Army from England. At the disposal of the Inspector of Army Aviation from 1.11.1919. Pilot of the Aviation Group of the North-Western Front. In January 1920, in the Commission for the Delivery of Aviati
2 CONC on Property to the Estonian authorities.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: brother of Gösta Bergbom (19.02.1877, Brought. Finnish Edition - 1913); sister Lea, married Haglund (30.05.1882, Bjorneborg, Finnish Edition - 1951).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT Boikov V. A brief biographical dictionary of officers, officials and employees of the White North-Western Army (1918 - 1920), Tallinn, 2009. p. 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Bergbom
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.theaerodrome.com/forum/at...tid=1720&stc=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Bergbom was born in 6.10.1884 in Pori. He attended military academy of Hamina and completed higher school examination in 1903. He worked as secretary in board of pilot since 1912 as lieutenant, 1913 in institute of hydrograph
2 CONC ic.
2 CONT In 1915 he left everything and left to St. Petersburg and commanded to flying school in France. He completed pilot license in Artois'n early 1916. He served in france and serbian air forces.
2 CONT In Serbia he wounded and lied in french military hospital for long time. Last information were from Riga and september 1919 from Tallinn - from Judenits army. He was presumably joined into Wrangel's army and killed in Crimea 1920.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.ra.ee/dgs/_purl.php?shc=ERA.957.16.1482:55 Saaga ERA.957.16.1482:55]
