1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jean Poirot, born on March 26 1873 in Andelot (Haute-Marne) and died in Paris May 20 1924, was a French phonetician and linguist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Vosgian descent, he is the son of Camille-Hippolyte Poirot, a 31-year-old hardware storekeeper, and Julie Girardon, 23 years old. He studied at the École normale supérieure from November 1893 to July 1898. He was influenced by 
2 CONC his philosophy teacher Henri Bergson (1859-1941) and Charles Andler (1866-1932), a lecturer in German.
2 CONT
